WEBVTT

00:08:00.768 --> 00:08:02.686
When we hear the word "deficit,"

00:08:02.686 --> 00:08:07.233
we probably think
of a deficiency or shortfall.

00:08:07.233 --> 00:08:10.486
A deficit always sounds ominous.

00:08:10.486 --> 00:08:13.239
So when we hear
that the federal government

00:08:13.239 --> 00:08:17.660
just ran a three-trillion-dollar
budget deficit,

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:19.328
it can sound worrying.

00:08:20.746 --> 00:08:22.581
And it can even anger people.

00:08:23.707 --> 00:08:27.795
But there's another way
to think about government deficits.

00:08:27.836 --> 00:08:33.092
Just as a six becomes a nine
when we view it from a different angle,